@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1742 = private unnamed_addr constant [18 x i8] c"useless-comparison", align 1
@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1743 = private unnamed_addr constant [829 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for useless comparisons.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUseless comparisons have no effect on the program, and are often included\0Aby mistake. If the comparison is intended to enforce an invariant, prepend\0Athe comparison with an `assert`. Otherwise, remove it entirely.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afoo == bar\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aassert foo == bar, \22`foo` and `bar` should be equal.\22\0A```\0A\0A## Notebook behavior\0AFor Jupyter Notebooks, this rule is not applied to the last top-level expression in a cell.\0AThis is because it's common to have a notebook cell that ends with an expression,\0Awhich will result in the `repr` of the evaluated expression being printed as the cell's output.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `assert` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-assert-statement)\0A", align 1
