@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.2059 = private unnamed_addr constant [15 x i8] c"if-expr-min-max", align 1
@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.2060 = private unnamed_addr constant [709 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `if` expressions that can be replaced with `min()` or `max()`\0Acalls.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAn `if` expression that selects the lesser or greater of two\0Asub-expressions can be replaced with a `min()` or `max()` call\0Arespectively. When possible, prefer `min()` and `max()`, as they're more\0Aconcise and readable than the equivalent `if` expression.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Ahighest_score = score1 if score1 > score2 else score2\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Ahighest_score = max(score2, score1)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `min`](https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#min)\0A- [Python documentation: `max`](https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#max)\0A", align 1
