@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.2083 = private unnamed_addr constant [18 x i8] c"if-key-in-dict-del", align 1
@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.2084 = private unnamed_addr constant [404 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `if key in dictionary: del dictionary[key]`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ATo remove a key-value pair from a dictionary, it's more concise to use `.pop(..., None)`.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aif key in dictionary:\0A    del dictionary[key]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Adictionary.pop(key, None)\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as safe, unless the if statement contains comments.\0A", align 1
