@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.2087 = private unnamed_addr constant [24 x i8] c"none-not-at-end-of-union", align 1
@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.2088 = private unnamed_addr constant [769 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for type annotations where `None` is not at the end of an union.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AType annotation unions are associative, meaning that the order of the elements\0Adoes not matter. The `None` literal represents the absence of a value. For\0Areadability, it's preferred to write the more informative type expressions first.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef func(arg: None | int): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef func(arg: int | None): ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Union type](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#types-union)\0A- [Python documentation: `typing.Optional`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Optional)\0A- [Python documentation: `None`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/constants.html#None)\0A", align 1
